          "target": "urn:uuid:1a2b3c4d-e6f7-46d2-8def-123456789103",
          "rationale": "Chest pain can be a symptom of acute coronary syndromes (ACS).",
          "citation": "Text mentions chest pain accounts for 5–10% of US emergency department visits and presentation of ACS is not always symptom specific.",
          "citation_paraphrase": "Text mentions chest pain accounts for 5–10% of US emergency department visits and presentation of ACS is not always symptom specific.",
          "citation_verbatim_excerpt": "This presentation is extremely time sensitive.Respiratory ConcernsThe high-risk patient is one who is currently ventilating and oxygenating adequately but is in respiratory distress and has the potential to rapidly deteriorate.",
          "citation_type": "paraphrase_with_recovered_excerpt"
        },
